# Tuning the loot

Every bin draws from the **Shared loot** list (**Items & loot** tab), unless you give a bin its own.

## How a search works

1. Each loot item is rolled on its own. An item with **Chance** 25 is found on one search in four.
2. Each item found gets a random amount between **Fewest** and **Most**.
3. If more than **Most items per search** were found, a random few are kept.
4. The bin is then empty for a random time between **Cooldown: shortest** and **Cooldown: longest** (**Timing & schedule** tab). This happens even when nothing was found.

## Add an item

1. Open `/poggy` → **Trash Bins** → **Items & loot**.
2. In **Shared loot**, press **Add loot item**.
3. Pick the **Item**. It must exist in your items table.
4. Set a **Label**, a **Chance** (1 to 100) and the **Fewest** and **Most**.
5. Save and restart.

## Make bins richer or poorer

| To | Change |
|---|---|
| Find more often | Raise the **Chance** of common items. |
| Find more per search | Raise **Most items per search**. |
| Search a bin more often | Lower the cooldowns (in seconds; 1800 is 30 minutes). |
| Stop players farming | Raise the cooldowns. |

## One bin with different loot

Open **Locations** → **Bins**, pick the bin, and fill its **Own loot (optional)** tab.
Every other bin keeps using the shared list.
